og x scaling across the 10^6 -> 10^7 measurement (extrapolation: ~25x at 10^9). **HL approximation polylog by construction, matches within 0.34 sigma_Pois at 6 cells**: HL_H(x;w) = C(H) * w / log^k(x) at (x_max, k) cells, mean |err/sigma_Pois| = 0.137 across 6 cells. Positive-direction polylog primitive on the k-tuple axis, analogous to Thread 7's R_K(x) and Thread 8's HL_inf(h, x). **What this rules out**: (i) strong H1 hypothesis "Thread-5-shape FAILS to transpose" — refuted, dichotomy transposes (REFINED to H1' bounded-by-sieve-baseline); (ii) hypothesis that speedup is x-independent within polylog regime — refuted, speedup grows with sqrt(x) / log scaling. **What this does NOT close**: (i) worst-case (pointwise) HL error bound — slot 2 target via cross-x ensemble; (ii) decade scaling beyond 10^7 — slot 2 target at 10^8 / 10^9; (iii) named-exponent error bound for HL_H(x; w) — slot 3+ target (cross-x analogue of Thread 8 HLRH); (iv) non-narrow windows w = x^delta. **Cites** E1.5 (cross-x analogue on k-tuple narrow-window axis), S195 (random-phase frame), S224 (Correlation Dichotomy template), S418 / S421 (Thread 8 EXACT/APPROX dichotomy + HL evaluator template transposed h-axis -> x-axis), Hardy-Littlewood 1923 k-tuple conjecture (singular-series formula), Tarjan 1985 amortised-analysis decomposition (T_per_x_amort = T_anchor/M + per-query floor — USED final at S224). **Cross-domain ingredient**: no new technique; reuses Thread-5 amortised-analysis decomposition. **Slot 2 recommendation** (highest yield): cross-x HL residual distribution analysis at fixed admissible H, varying x in narrow window — analogue of Thread 8 slot 2's cross-h ensemble at fixed x. Targets: half-Gaussian KS shape, sigma_eff/sigma_pois suppression factor, decade-stability check; building toward Thread-8-shape conditional named-exponent theorem on cross-x k-tuple axis at slot 4/5. See `experiments/analytic/k_tuple_batched/{slot1_baseline.py, slot1_baseline.csv (72 rows), slot1_hl_compare.csv